(7623759, 1234847, 28742, '<td valign="top">Great job, Roz. Always would be nice to know why people vote less than 5 on images like this. I think it''s great. Perspective gives the feeling of standing against the wall, maybe hiding... from the cops... uh oh, they released the K9 unit! <br/>10th is pretty good and a PH to boot! :)</td>', 'Great job, Roz. Always would be nice to know why people vote less than 5 on images like this. I think it''s great. Perspective gives the feeling of standing against the wall, maybe hiding... from the cops... uh oh, they released the K9 unit! 10th is pretty good and a PH to boot! :)', '2019-04-07 15:22:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7623781, 1234847, 16148, '<td valign="top">F16 was a good choice.   I love that you revealed all the details by closing down the aperture.  We were even treated to a star burst!  Thanks to your posthumous award I stumbled on your photograph.  Great work!</td>', 'F16 was a good choice.   I love that you revealed all the details by closing down the aperture.  We were even treated to a star burst!  Thanks to your posthumous award I stumbled on your photograph.  Great work!', '2019-04-07 18:00:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7623831, 1234938, 182284, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! What a beautiful shot.</td>', 'Congratulations! What a beautiful shot.', '2019-04-08 00:10:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7623969, 1234847, 124815, '<td valign="top">I neglected to vote. Hard to figure out exactly how I would have marked. I did not look at the others. Never mind.<br/>Probably 8. I liked it more on instagram. Here I get a bit lost visually. Too much great information for just two eyes. And I really can''t crop it. This awful feeling that something is really good but....<br/> <br/>As a side note, I find funny if not too dangerous your risky way to take this shot but in a work on art nobody cares if it was done in 3 years or 3 hours. No fairness!!!!!</td>', 'I neglected to vote. Hard to figure out exactly how I would have marked. I did not look at the others. Never mind.Probably 8. I liked it more on instagram. Here I get a bit lost visually. Too much great information for just two eyes. And I really can''t crop it. This awful feeling that something is really good but.... As a side note, I find funny if not too dangerous your risky way to take this shot but in a work on art nobody cares if it was done in 3 years or 3 hours. No fairness!!!!!', '2019-04-08 15:33:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7623971, 1234759, 30861, '<td valign="top">I drove through Little Rock in 1969, emphasis on "through", but I never have spent any time in Arkansas, spiffster, so you got away with this one :-)</td>', 'I drove through Little Rock in 1969, emphasis on "through", but I never have spent any time in Arkansas, spiffster, so you got away with this one :-)', '2019-04-08 16:36:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7624006, 1234900, 83313, '<td valign="top">No wonder it looks so similar. Not the same fort, but I looked up Fort Pulaski and it is very similar in design to Fort Barrancas, both inside and outside.<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1191332" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2019-04-08 20:42:05.</i></td>', 'No wonder it looks so similar. Not the same fort, but I looked up Fort Pulaski and it is very similar in design to Fort Barrancas, both inside and outside.', '2019-04-08 21:40:28.000000', '2019-04-08 21:42:05.000000', 0),
(7624036, 1234900, 33515, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> No wonder it looks so similar. Not the same fort, but I looked up Fort Pulaski and it is very similar in design to Fort Barrancas, both inside and outside.<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1191332" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2381/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1191332.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, Fort Barrancas is a Third System Fort as well, I will be visiting there this week. While they have similar looks they are quite different forts, Barrancas is a combination of a Third System Fort and a modernized Spanish Battery. Barrancas is a great fort to visit.</td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: No wonder it looks so similar. Not the same fort, but I looked up Fort Pulaski and it is very similar in design to Fort Barrancas, both inside and outside.  Yes, Fort Barrancas is a Third System Fort as well, I will be visiting there this week. While they have similar looks they are quite different forts, Barrancas is a combination of a Third System Fort and a modernized Spanish Battery. Barrancas is a great fort to visit.', '2019-04-09 07:32:34.000000', NULL, 0),
